---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';

const credits = [
  ['SVGO', 'https://github.com/svg/svgo', 'tidies every file', 'MIT'],
  ['DOMPurify', 'https://github.com/cure53/DOMPurify', 'strips anything unsafe', 'MPL-2.0 or Apache-2.0'],
  ['Mediabunny', 'https://mediabunny.dev', 'writes MP4', 'MPL-2.0'],
  ['gifenc', 'https://github.com/mattdesl/gifenc', 'writes GIF', 'MIT'],
  ['Zod', 'https://zod.dev', 'checks every saved animation', 'MIT'],
  ['idb-keyval', 'https://github.com/jakearchibald/idb-keyval', 'keeps your last file in this browser', 'Apache-2.0'],
  ['Astro', 'https://astro.build', 'builds the site', 'MIT'],
  ['Svelte', 'https://svelte.dev', 'runs the editor', 'MIT'],
  ['Tailwind CSS', 'https://tailwindcss.com', 'styles it', 'MIT'],
  ['daisyUI', 'https://daisyui.com', 'styles it too', 'MIT'],
];
---

<Page title="About" description="What Animated SVG GO does, how it works, where the code lives and who it builds on.">
  <div class="flex max-w-3xl flex-col gap-8">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold">About</h1>
    <p class="text-lg">
      A free tool for bringing an SVG to life. Think <a class="link" href="https://jakearchibald.github.io/svgomg/">SVGOMG</a>, but for
      motion.
    </p>

    <section aria-labelledby="what-heading" class="flex flex-col gap-2">
      <h2 id="what-heading" class="text-xl font-bold">What it does</h2>
      <p>
        Drop in a file, choose shapes, add effects, export. There are nine effects: Spin, Fade, Draw, Pop, Float, Wiggle, Pulse, Slide in
        and Colour shift. Stack them, stagger them, pick an easing, drag the pivot and scrub the timeline. Undo and redo work as you'd
        expect.
      </p>
      <p>
        Take it out as an animated SVG, an SVG with CSS or JavaScript to paste into a page, a GIF or an MP4. The SVG, CSS and JavaScript
        exports respect reduced motion settings.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="how-heading" class="flex flex-col gap-2">
      <h2 id="how-heading" class="text-xl font-bold">How it works</h2>
      <p>
        Your file is tidied, then cleaned of scripts and anything else that could run. It is shown in a locked-down frame that can't run
        code. Each effect becomes plain CSS keyframes, so what you see in the editor is what you export. GIF and MP4 are drawn frame by
        frame from the same timeline. All of it happens on your machine. No uploads, no accounts.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="source-heading" class="flex flex-col gap-2">
      <h2 id="source-heading" class="text-xl font-bold">Open source</h2>
      <p>
        The code is on <a class="link" href="https://github.com/ddools/animated-svg-go">GitHub</a> under the MIT licence. Found a bug, or
        a file that won't load? <a class="link" href="https://github.com/ddools/animated-svg-go/issues">Open an issue</a>. Attach the SVG if
        you can.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="next-heading" class="flex flex-col gap-2">
      <h2 id="next-heading" class="text-xl font-bold">What's next</h2>
      <p>Path morphing, so one shape can turn into another. Then share links.</p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="who-heading" class="flex flex-col gap-2">
      <h2 id="who-heading" class="text-xl font-bold">Who made it</h2>
      <p>Der Dooley.</p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="browsers-heading" class="flex flex-col gap-2">
      <h2 id="browsers-heading" class="text-xl font-bold">Browsers</h2>
      <p>Chrome, Firefox and Safari on a desktop or laptop. Phones and tablets aren't supported yet.</p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="credits-heading" class="flex flex-col gap-2">
      <h2 id="credits-heading" class="text-xl font-bold">Built on</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-6">
        {
          credits.map(([name, href, job, licence]) => (
            <li>
              <a class="link" href={href}>{name}</a> {job}. {licence}.
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ul>
    </section>
  </div>
</Page>
